  "metadata": {
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D1_nonuniform_dirichlet_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The plain match D(u,x) must fire through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint (default priority) and lower to the rule's makearray -- interior [2,7] holding the imported 3-point centered nonuniform first-derivative stencil aggregate, faces i=1 and i=8 holding the second-order fixed-value Dirichlet wall closures -- with all metaparameters folded, all apply_expression_template nodes inlined (including the two grid geometry templates the observeds xc and dxw apply to the node array xe), the free-name geometry arrays xc and dxw surviving as index references, and the free-name wall values gL, gR surviving as bare name references in the two face terms. The model declares gL and gR as ordinary real parameters (gL = 0 homogeneous, gR = 1 nonzero) so both the homogeneous and the inhomogeneous wall term appear in the expanded golden; parameters are not metaparameter-folded, so gL/gR stay as names (a consuming model that omits them falls back to the default 0). The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at N=8: it supplies the 9-node (x_nodes) quadratic-stretch array xe and derives xc = nonuniform_cell_center(xe), dxw = nonuniform_cell_width(xe), all spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N. The Dirichlet first-derivative closure reads the half control-width dxw/2 as the center-to-wall distance, so dxw is materialized (unlike the zero-gradient first-derivative fixture). The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST -- including the grid-derived geometry observeds -- across bindings.",
